+ * ambiguous, because the leading param may absorb the separator
+ * (`match("/:a-:b")("/a-b-c")` gives `a = "a-b"`), and every formulation
+ * `recheck` rates safe changes which strings the pattern matches. Filed and
+ * blocked as PTR-2, with the semantic choice under Proposed. An entry that
+ * turns safe fails this suite too: the exception has then outlived its cause
+ * and belongs back in the gate.
